{"nodes": [{"id": "tools_test_linked_the_other_page", "label": "The other page (link target fixture)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_link_following", "label": "Six things that have to work to arrive here", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The layout kept its boxes, the click was turned into a point on the page, link_at found the run under it, the relative address was resolved against the one the browser was on, and the whole fetch happened again. The only way to know all six work is to arrive here."}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_link_at", "label": "link_at", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Finds the laid-out run under a clicked point."}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_layout_runs", "label": "Layout keeps its runs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A word is where a font change, a link's hit rectangle and a selection all attach. That is why layout keeps its runs."}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_cascade_missing", "label": "The cascade parses and nothing asks it", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "libcss parses, selects and answers, and nothing asks it. Colour, font size, weight and slant should come from the computed style rather than from the tag's name."}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_box_model_missing", "label": "No box model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Blocks are stacked and inline content flows; everything else about geometry is a constant in a header."}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_images_missing", "label": "Images - plumbing rather than a decoder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "stb_image is already vendored for the PDF reader."}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_forms_missing", "label": "Forms - a box that takes keys", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It needs boxes to be addressable from outside the layout - the same step that made the link clickable."}, {"id": "tools_test_linked_back_button", "label": "Back button and link are two ways to the same place", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The return link is also a link, so both paths have to work."}], "edges": [{"source": "tools_test_linked_the_other_page", "target": "tools_test_page_layout_test_page", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "tools_test_linked_link_following", "target": "tools_test_linked_link_at", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "tools/test_linked.html", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "tools_test_linked_link_following", "target": "tools_test_linked_layout_runs", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "co